Say whether a block enumeration was handed a nil element.

An element that IS nil and an element whose property ANSWERS nil are the same crash from the
callers side. iA Writer raises Cannot remove a nil key inside a block that
enumerateObjectsWithOptions: drives, and nothing above that line can tell the two apart: a message
to nil answers nil, so [nil identifier] and [realObject identifier] with an unset ivar arrive at
removeObjectForKey: identically.

CIDER_TRACE_ENUM prints one line per enumeration with the count, the options, how many elements
were nil, the index of the first one and the class of element zero. One line per call keeps it
cheap enough to leave on for a five minute drive.

It announces itself on the first call, so silence means the method was never reached rather than
the switch was never read.

